Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mm: count shrinkable GPU pool pages in MemAvailable

The GPU driver keeps pages it has finished with in a pool for
reuse. They hold no data and are freed on demand, but MemAvailable
does not count them. On an APU this pool can reach several GiB, so
tools that compute 'used = MemTotal - MemAvailable' report memory
as used when it is really free for the taking.

Add the pool (NR_GPU_RECLAIM) to the estimate.

Some drivers over-report NR_GPU_RECLAIM (it has been seen above
MemTotal), so cap the result at MemTotal minus the reserves. Tools
that compute 'used = MemTotal - MemAvailable' then never go negative.

---
diff --git a/Documentation/filesystems/proc.rst b/Documentation/filesystems/proc.rst
index 2ccd5b2..a53387c 100644
--- a/Documentation/filesystems/proc.rst
+++ b/Documentation/filesystems/proc.rst
@@ -1126,8 +1126,8 @@ MemFree
 MemAvailable
               An estimate of how much memory is available for starting new
               applications, without swapping. Calculated from MemFree,
-              SReclaimable, the size of the file LRU lists, and the low
-              watermarks in each zone.
+              SReclaimable, GPUReclaim, the size of the file LRU lists,
+              and the low watermarks in each zone.
               The estimate takes into account that the system needs some
               page cache to function well, and that not all reclaimable
               slab will be reclaimable, due to items being in use. The
diff --git a/mm/show_mem.c b/mm/show_mem.c
index 43aca5a..2b9dbdc 100644
--- a/mm/show_mem.c
+++ b/mm/show_mem.c
@@ -66,6 +66,9 @@ long si_mem_available(void)
 	reclaimable -= min(reclaimable / 2, wmark_low);
 	available += reclaimable;
 
+	available += global_node_page_state(NR_GPU_RECLAIM);
+	available = min_t(long, available, totalram_pages() - totalreserve_pages);
+
 	if (available < 0)
 		available = 0;
 	return available;
